The [[Frostbite]] is a neutral [[Weapon]] normally obtained by combining a [[Hungry Blade]] with a [[Snowball]], although a [[Pyromancer]] with [[Frozen Flame]] could also find it in the shop. It is a more powerful {{icon/cold}}-themed variant of the [[Hungry Blade]]. On hit, it has a chance to inflict 1 {{icon/cold}}, and deals more damage the more {{icon/vampirism}} the player has and the more {{icon/cold}} the opponent has. Rather than the slow conversion of {{icon/regeneration}} into {{icon/vampirism}} used by the [[Hungry Blade]], the [[Frostbite]] generates a large amount of {{icon/vampirism}} once the opponent reaches a high enough {{icon/cold}} threshold.

The [[Hungry Blade]] only gains maximum damage from {{icon/vampirism}}, while the [[Frostbite]] gains general damage, meaning it scales about twice as well with {{icon/vampirism}}, not to mention the added effect of {{icon/cold}}-scaling. Since the [[Hungry Blade]] would likely generate more {{icon/vampirism}} outside of a {{icon/cold}} build, there are likely some niche builds where the [[Hungry Blade]] is actually better, but the [[Frostbite]] will usually be better and has a much higher ceiling when incorporated into a high {{icon/vampirism}} or high {{icon/cold}} build.
